 :notes
 ["Component status includes the partial local assessment continuation; the existing Agora M4 and artifact-trace capabilities remain done, and the four optional continuations remain future."
  "P013-AE-001 qualifies only the bounded common local view on a generic open resource reference; P013-AE-002 and the full Whisper curation, propagation and attention workflow remain planned."
  "Whisper intake/redaction is a supervised channel_json middleware service with a separately owned intake/trace/operator HTTP surface; shared transport-independent semantics belong in `whisper-core`."
  "Post-M4 productization adds a host-owned provider-policy shape for Inquirium/model-runtime redaction providers and a secretless simulator acceptance bridge without making adapters publication authorities."
  "P090-006e binds exact observed-result bytes and retains private result/draft readback; unknown ancestry, full Memarium transport/recovery and deferred/terminal lifecycle qualification remain explicit gaps."
  "Planned continuations reuse one epoch pull executor, a contextual contribution evaluator with separate coordination/disclosure policies, one ordered case owner and P015/P035 proof verification; Artifact Delivery owns delivery and retry. Proposed DTO details and trackers remain with the linked proposal owners, not additional implemented capabilities."
  "Transport qualification belongs to P035-007/009/010 and does not qualify every Whisper/issuance flow, homeserver federation, independent backups or production readiness."
  "`whisper-core` carries production-shaped source, routing, privacy, correlation, association-room, and public-gossip promotion contracts; concrete UI and relay runtime layers consume those contracts later."
  "Callers of outbound privacy should declare intent, not name a concrete relay module."
  "Agora M4 uses Story-005 as the three-node public/federated smoke: node A and node B submit similar sanitized signals, node C runs the Agora relay/server, and threshold/proposal state is rebuilt from accepted public records."]}
